# Resource: monad_enrichment

An enrichment sits between other nodes in a pipeline and adds context to every record: a join against a KV Lookup table you populate yourself, or a call to an external provider such as GreyNoise or a geolocation service (see the [enrichments catalog](https://app.monad.com/docs/enrichments)). Each enrichment extracts a value from the record at a **join path**, looks it up, and writes the result under a **destination key** as a small envelope (`join_key`, `code`, `message`, `data`).

Like inputs and outputs, an enrichment has a **type** and a **config** of settings and credentials, and it processes records only once a `monad_pipeline` names it in an `enrichment` node.

